From s.henderson at ucl.ac.uk  Tue Jul  3 13:20:53 2007
From: s.henderson at ucl.ac.uk (Stephen Henderson)
Date: Tue, 3 Jul 2007 12:20:53 +0100
Subject: [BioC] SAM algorithm S0 value calculation
Message-ID: <61B482B74D6EE443B90356E080476E34DEE56F@exc2.cruciform.wibr.ucl.ac.uk>

In the original paper:
"Significance analysis of microarrays applied to the ionizing radiation
response". PNAS 2001 98: 5116-5121, (Apr 24).

The calculation of s0 is described thus (page 2, first column):
"The coefficient of variance of d(i) was computed as a function of s(i)
in moving windows across the data. The value of s0 was chosen to
minimize the coefficient of variance"

s(i) is the measured standard deviation.
d(i)  is their relative difference score with s(i) + s0 in the
denominator.


