Dear Holger and Gordon,

Thanks a lot for your responses - that is very helpful. It is likely that
both ways of calculating fold change are correct, but I agree with Gordon
that it is most appropriate to report the fold change that was used to
generate the significance statistic.

I was also thinking I could take the fold changes calculated by both methods
and go with the largest (arrays seem to underestimate the magnitude of the
fold change), but this would have the issue that merging them would not
maintain the same confidence. Ultimately going with the fold change used for
the statistic will be the simplest approach.

Thanks again for your responses.

Best wishes,

Peter

